---
title: "Planning — Manifest Then Reason Backward"
scope: global
---
flowchart TD
    INTENT["PROJECT INTENT<br/>Brief + taste profile + capabilities"]

    subgraph PHASE_A["Phase A: MANIFESTATION — runs through sensory cortex"]
        A1["Each active sense manifests<br/>what must be true about<br/>the finished artifact"]
        A2["Design: 'dark/bold visual<br/>language, card-based layout'"]
        A3["Systems: 'sub-2s load,<br/>lazy images, CDN-ready'"]
        A4["Security: 'CSP headers,<br/>input sanitized, no exposed keys'"]
        A5["Motor Cortex synthesizes<br/>all perspectives into a<br/>MANIFESTED FUTURE"]
        A6["Senses evaluate:<br/>does this future satisfy intent?<br/>Tensions resolved HERE,<br/>before any task planning"]
        A7["MANIFESTED FUTURE<br/>Concrete, reason-backward-from-able<br/>shared vision for the project"]
    end

    subgraph PHASE_B["Phase B: BACKWARD PATH REASONING"]
        B1["LLM reasons backward:<br/>'To get THERE, what must<br/>exist just before? And before that?'"]
        B2["Jensen's THREE NECESSITY GATES<br/>applied to every proposed task"]
        B3{"Does this task<br/>need to exist?"}
        B4{"Does it need to be<br/>exactly this?"}
        B5{"Does it need to<br/>take this long?"}
        B6["TASK GRAPH<br/>Minimum viable path<br/>with dependencies +<br/>phase groups"]
    end

    INTENT --> A1
    A1 --> A2 & A3 & A4
    A2 & A3 & A4 --> A5 --> A6 --> A7
    A7 --> B1 --> B2 --> B3
    B3 -->|no| CUT["Cut task"]
    B3 -->|yes| B4
    B4 -->|no| SIMPLIFY["Simplify task"]
    B4 -->|yes| B5
    B5 -->|no| COMPRESS["Compress task"]
    B5 -->|yes| B6

    style PHASE_A fill:#e8e0f0,stroke:#7c6af0,color:#1a1a2e
    style PHASE_B fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669,color:#1a1a2e
    style A7 fill:#fef9c3,stroke:#ca8a04,color:#1a1a2e
    style CUT fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#f87171,color:#1a1a2e
    style SIMPLIFY fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#f87171,color:#1a1a2e
    style COMPRESS fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#f87171,color:#1a1a2e
    style B6 fill:#fef9c3,stroke:#ca8a04,color:#1a1a2e
